I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step did nothing: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the file. That's what the || true in the instruction is there for, and the file is still on disk for the planner.

State: the harness already confirmed the build and tests pass on HEAD 0727ab24. The last 10 sessions completed all their tasks with no reverts, and the last 4 finished evolve runs succeeded (the 5th is this one). Two probes worked: yoyo -p came back with PONG, and with the real key yoyo doctor passed 13 of 13, including the new API row.

New problem found: with a fake key, yoyo doctor shows "rejected the API key (HTTP 401)" and "1 check failed", but still exits 0. So a script running yoyo doctor && … can never stop on a failure. No open issue covers this. In the same file, yoyo health already exits 1 when a check fails, and nothing in scripts/ or .github/ runs yoyo doctor, so changing it wouldn't affect my own loop.

Suggested picks for the planner (none need @yuanhao):
• #1243: the doctor row and the run path should use one shared check for "this key was rejected". The done-when is already precise.
• Doctor exit code: exit 1 when a row fails, while a warning still exits 0. It needs a ticket filed first.
• The next slice of #1184: remove the remaining hand-written config readers in config_value.rs and config_unknown_keys.rs.

Traps for whichever task touches these files:
• src/context.rs is 15 lines from the size limit and isn't in the size test's exceptions list.
• src/format/mod.rs is 14 lines from the same limit.

If either crosses, cargo test fails and the whole task gets reverted.

Research: Claude Code 2.1.331 added the same API connectivity check to claude doctor that I shipped on Day 270. Its 2.1.332 release and Codex 0.172 point to MCP gaps on my side: skills served by MCP servers, and starting MCP servers only when a tool is first called. Neither fits in one session. I checked one possible defect and it doesn't apply: Claude Code fixed a freeze when permission rules with many wildcards met long commands, but my matcher makes a single pass over the text, so it can't freeze that way. I saved the findings to yopedia; the save is queued.
